id: pm-gzr4j6
title: "Ecosystem Daily Release jobs hold a hosted runner for up to 360 minutes waiting on their own release PR's queued CI, and ecosystem CI never cancels superseded runs, so the account's 20 runner slots starve every repository"
description: "About 30 ecosystem repositories (pm-rl, pm-ops, pm-presets, pm-swarm, pm-ts-starter, pm-changelog, ...) schedule release.yml at the same cron minute (23 3 * * *, pm-changelog 17 3). Its release job opens a release PR and then waits in-job (merge wait 60-120 minutes, job timeout 360) for that PR's CI, holding a GitHub-hosted runner while the CI it waits for is queued behind the same held runners. Ecosystem ci.yml has no concurrency group, so every push to a PR branch queues another full Node 22/26 (and sometimes Windows) matrix without cancelling the superseded run. All repositories share the personal account's 20 concurrent-job cap, so this starves pm-cli and every other repository for hours. The fix belongs in the ecosystem release and CI templates, not in pm-cli."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: ci,ecosystem,github-actions,release,runner-queue
created_at: "2026-10-30T15:20:19.395Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T17:14:11.623Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: No ecosystem release workflow job polls or sleeps for its release PR's checks while holding a runner; publication is triggered by the merge event; Every ecosystem ci.yml declares concurrency group per workflow and ref with cancel-in-progress for pull_request events; Ecosystem release crons are spread over distinct minutes so no two repositories start a release in the same 5-minute window; An account-wide snapshot one hour after the release window shows no in-progress Daily Release run waiting on its own PR
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: GitHub Free personal account unbraind shared by about 30 public repositories
expected_result: "A daily release never holds a runner while waiting for review or CI: the release job enables auto-merge (or exits) and a separate pull_request closed/workflow_run trigger publishes; ecosystem CI declares concurrency with cancel-in-progress for pull_request refs; release crons are staggered across repositories."
actual_result: "Snapshot 2026-10-30T15:08Z: 60 active workflow runs across the account, 47 queued; 5 Daily Release runs in progress since 10:09-13:37Z all inside 'Run release checks' / merge wait, 7 more queued; pm-ts-starter had 3 CI runs queued for one PR branch (fix/min-sdk-drift-check). pm-cli PR #1629 waited 94 minutes for its first job."
component: ecosystem-release
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-m6ig79,related,"2026-10-30T15:20:19.395Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-30T17:14:11.623Z","harness:claude-code","2026-10-30 17:15 UTC queue census across all unbraind repos: about 90 queued runs against the 20-job account cap and zero pm-cli jobs in progress. 45 of the queued runs were Dependabot dynamic update jobs, mostly repeats of the same directory update (PersonalAgent pip 10+10, arXiv-PyG-new uv 7, Tokenwerk uv 5). Cancelled the 31 superseded queued Dependabot runs, keeping the newest per repository and directory. Repeated Dependabot update jobs are a second source of runner starvation beside the release merge waits; a durable fix needs grouped Dependabot updates or open-pull-request limits in those repositories."
body: ""
